invariant: INV-14
file: srv_parser.c
catches: srv_test
reason: srv_ext_over_max answers 1 at SRV_CLIENT_HELLO_EXT_MAX extensions
  rather than past it, so the parser refuses a ClientHello of exactly 128,
  which srv_parser.h states it accepts. This is the lower side of the
  boundary pair: test/srv_parser_reader_tests.h fills the golden hello out
  to the bound and requires it to parse, with a frozen digest over every
  covered extension.

--- old
        if (count > SRV_CLIENT_HELLO_EXT_MAX) {
--- new
        if (count >= SRV_CLIENT_HELLO_EXT_MAX) {
